    <string name="eq_text_21">Engine resampling</string>
    <string name="eq_text_22">Choose how the engine converts its 11,025 Hz audio. Sinc filters spectral replicas without adding acoustic information. Follow quality preserves automatic selection.</string>
    <string name="eq_text_23">Output frequency is not bit depth. Audio is 16-bit PCM. The usual source is 11,025 Hz, with a theoretical frequency limit of 5,512.5 Hz. 22,050, 24,000 and 32,000 Hz outputs are resampled. Sinc is recommended to filter spectral replicas.</string>
    <string name="interface_text_1">Interface mode</string>
    <string name="interface_text_3">Standard</string>
    <string name="interface_text_4">Expert</string>
    <string name="interface_text_5">Standard shows explanations. Expert keeps names, values and accessible controls with less text.</string>
    <string name="notification_text_1">Notification customization</string>
    <string name="notification_text_2">Two buttons adjust the chosen parameter; the third stops speech and noise. Changes apply to upcoming sentences. Speed, pitch and language chosen here override the requesting app.</string>
    <string name="notification_text_3">Show engine notification</string>
    <string name="notification_text_4">Allow this app’s notifications in Android to see controls.</string>
    <string name="notification_text_5">Enable customizable controls</string>
    <string name="notification_text_6">Notification parameter</string>
    <string name="notification_text_7">TTS output ear</string>
    <string name="notification_text_9">Left only</string>
    <string name="notification_text_10">Both</string>
    <string name="notification_text_11">Right only</string>
    <string name="notification_text_12">Only engine audio is changed. Music and videos keep their balance. Android may mix channels when mono audio is enabled.</string>
    <string name="notification_text_13">Wireless maintenance with white noise</string>
    <string name="notification_text_14">Experimental, initially off. Requires an active notification and app playback through Accessibility or Media. Keeps stereo Bluetooth active between synthesis requests, including with the screen off, up to the selected limit. Each utterance restarts the timer. Stops during speech, disconnection or calls. May reduce device wake-up time; does not remove codec delay.</string>
    <string name="notification_text_15">Maximum noise level</string>
    <string name="notification_text_16">Maintenance limit without speech synthesis</string>
    <string name="notification_text_17">Stop and disable wireless noise</string>
    <string name="notification_text_18">Stop speech and noise now</string>
    <string name="settings_text_1">Install Principal and Auxiliar. They are separate apps with their own settings, process and synthesis queue.</string>
    <string name="settings_text_2">If your screen reader follows Android’s default engine, select Principal in the system and Auxiliar in the other app. If the reader lets you choose an engine, assign Auxiliar to it and keep Principal for other apps.</string>
    <string name="settings_text_3">Apps using only the default engine share its queue. The engine cannot change their selection. Android and apps may mix audio or reduce volume.</string>
